            "content": "\u003Cdiv class=\"riddle2-wrapper\" data-is-qzzr=\"false\" data-rid-id=\"RHs3ooz0\" data-auto-scroll=\"true\" data-is-fixed-height-enabled=\"false\" data-bg=\"#fff\" data-fg=\"#00205b\" style=\"margin:0 auto; max-width:100%; width:640px;\" \u003E\u003Cscript src=\"https://www.riddle.com/embed/build-embedjs/embedV2.js\"\u003E\u003C/script\u003E\u003Ciframe title=\"Weekender Oct 10, 2026\" src=\"https://www.riddle.com/embed/a/RHs3ooz0?lazyImages=false&staticHeight=false\" allow=\"autoplay\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin\"\u003E\u003Csection data-block=\"SingleChoice\"\u003E\u003Ch2\u003EWhat is the process called when plants release water vapour through tiny openings in their leaves?\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003ETranspiration\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EAspiration\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ERespiration\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPerspiration\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection data-block=\"TextEntry\"\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EWhich five-letter word can go AFTER &quot;blue&quot;, &quot;finger&quot; and &quot;news&quot; to make three other words?\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003Eprint\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003Eprint.\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection data-block=\"SingleChoice\"\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EWho painted Guernica?\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPablo Picasso\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ESalvador Dali\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection data-block=\"SingleChoice\"\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EWhich element has the chemical symbol W?\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003ETungsten\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003ELead\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPotassium\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003EIron\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003C/section\u003E\u003Csection data-block=\"SingleChoice\"\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EIn the popular tongue-twister, who picked a peck of pickled peppers?\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003EPeter Piper\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E